  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "Inflation in most rich countries is a few percent. In the worst-hit countries right now, it's a different universe.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "chartUp"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "The 10 worst",
            "inflations now."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "At the top of the board today, prices are rising by well over five hundred percent a year.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "500%+",
          "label": "yearly inflation, worst countries",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Inflation is the steady rise in the average price of goods.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-inflation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · inflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And history's record is almost unimaginable. Zimbabwe once hit seventy-nine billion percent in a single month.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "79,000,000,000%",
          "label": "Zimbabwe's peak monthly rate",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Hyperinflation is when prices spiral completely out of control.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-hyperinflation",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · hyperinflation"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "At even fifty percent a month, cash loses about ninety-nine percent of its value in a year.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "crashChart",
          "big": "–99%/yr",
          "label": "at 50% monthly inflation",
          "props": [
            "chartDown",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It happens when the money supply explodes faster than goods.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-qtm",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · quantity theory of money"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "When their money dies, people flee to one thing above all, the US dollar.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "They flee to the dollar",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "When a currency collapses, savings, salaries, and whole middle classes can vanish within months.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "red",
          "line": "Middle class vanishes",
          "props": [
            "fire",
            "chartDown"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "It almost always tips into a full currency crisis.",
